<title>USA: McDonald's 1996 advertising expense up.</title>
<headline>McDonald's 1996 advertising expense up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonald's Corp said its advertising expenses totaled $503.3 million in 1996, up from $431.0 million in 1995 and $385.6 million in 1994.</p>
<p>In a recent Securities and Exchange Comission filing, the fast food giant said its focus in 1997 will be to increase sales at existing restaurants through aggressive marketing, a national value initiative, improved food taste, better service and improved facilities.</p>
<p>The company has said it will start a new price promotion in April, offering featured sandwiches for $0.55 each when french fries and a drink are also purchased.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
